  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2c11ca93ae4c81441b331ed9be64868a, type: 3}
  m_Name: Debrief_M2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: LastSignal.Core::LastSignal.DebriefCard
  title: Redundancy, and why risk numbers must reach the crew
  concept: Reliability of series systems and redundancy
  nasaSource: 'NASA Systems Engineering Handbook, NASA/SP-2016-6105 Rev2 [person
    6: confirm section]'
  body: 'If every subsystem must work, their chances multiply: five parts at 63%
    give about 10%. A backup unit raises one subsystem from r to 1 - (1 - r)^n, at
    the cost of mass. Real programs also make sure the crew sees the risk number.
    Reliabilities in this game are game-balance values, not NASA data.'
